  "description_short": "Laid-back beach bar on the Featherbed Nature Reserve with lagoon views and casual coastal vibes.",
  "description_long": "Perched on the shores of the Knysna Lagoon within the Featherbed Nature Reserve, this beach bar offers a refreshingly relaxed escape from the bustle of town. Accessible only by ferry, it's a destination worth the journey for those seeking cold drinks, simple bar snacks, and uninterrupted lagoon views. The setting is pure coastal charm — think sandy floors, wooden decks, and the sound of water lapping at the shore.\n\nThe menu keeps things straightforward with burgers, toasted sandwiches, and shareable platters that pair well with an ice-cold beer or sundowner cocktail. It's a popular spot for groups and families who've spent the day exploring the nature trails or simply soaking up the scenery. The atmosphere is casual and unpretentious, making it an ideal place to unwind after a hike or boat trip.\n\nWhether you're stopping by after the Featherbed ferry cruise or making it a dedicated outing, the bar captures that easy-going Garden Route spirit. It's not fine dining — it's a proper beach bar experience with one of the best views Knysna has to offer.",
